abstract: "On unmodified 3D incompressible Navier–Stokes, the geometric-kernel expansion of the two-point strain–direction pairing stops at C_CZ M(t)|δξ|² plus named remainders (A)–(C). Replacing the coefficient by an M-independent −γ is equivalent to the regularity problem. Explicit non-claim: this note does not prove global regularity and does not discharge the Constantin–Fefferman hypothesis."
